{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1270,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# Nex-N2.5-Pro — model  \n`Qwen3_5MoeForConditionalGeneration`: same config as **Qwen3.5-397B-A17B**, post-trained by Nex-AGI (Nex-N2-Pro's card names that base; the N2.5 card says it builds on N2). One continuous decoder-only stack L0–59, read top → bottom; layers that repeat are drawn once with **×N** (the barcode on the right lists every layer in order). **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel); **boxes = operations**. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one layer in detail."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1270,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Layer rows — **Gated DeltaNet** (45 layers, linear attention, fixed-size state) · **gated attention** (15 layers, every 4th, softmax + KV cache). Every layer then runs the same MoE: router picks **10 of 512** experts (SwiGLU, 1024 wide) plus 1 always-on **shared expert**.    \nLayer ≈ **6.58B** (DeltaNet) / **6.56B** (attention), 98% of it routed experts. Routed experts are stored FP8 (128×128 block scales); everything else BF16. Context 262 144 tokens."
  },
  {
   "id": "raw1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -960,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**raw text**  \"The cat sat…\"",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
